    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Intel Corp is a public company traded under the ticker INTC, headquartered in Santa Clara, California, and registered with the SEC under CIK 0000050863. Its website presents the company under the line \"Intel Inside - Built for AI\" and describes its offering as delivering AI at scale across cloud, data center, edge, and client with hardware and software solutions. The site also highlights a Googlebook built on an Intel platform, which it describes as engineering performance, graphics, battery, and connectivity to work as one.\n\nThe company's stated AI position is broad rather than tied to a single product: it frames AI as something to be delivered across cloud, data center, edge, and client environments through combined hardware and software. The site carries standard cautions that Intel technologies may require enabled hardware, software, or service activation, that no product or component can be absolutely secure, and that costs, results, and performance vary by use and configuration. It also states that Intel is committed to respecting human rights and avoiding adverse human rights impacts, and that its products and software are intended only for applications that do not cause or contribute to such impacts.\n\nOn the litigation side, Intel's recorded exposure sits in California, with 281 cases counted there. No other cases are listed.",
